summary:
  The heading's pulse asks Plasma's popup whether the face is on screen.

history:
  The face's animations ran while root.expanded was true, which is the
  popup and nothing else. With the face in a window of its own the popup
  is shut: the pulse under the station's name would stand still there, and
  run on in a popup that only holds a placeholder. Every such place reads
  root.faceShown.

target:
  package/contents/ui/Heading.qml

find:
                  running: isPlaying() && root.faceShown && !root.thrifty

replace:
                  running: isPlaying() && root.expanded && !root.thrifty

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_the_face_asks_whether_it_is_on_screen_in_one_place.
